    "lawCode": "Add §13-0340-h, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S9463\n\nSPONSOR: HARCKHAM\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to\nestablishing the authority of the department of environmental conserva-\ntion to manage Atlantic bonito and false albacore\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo establish the DEC's authority to manage Atlantic bonito and false\nalbacore.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one amends the environmental conservation law by adding a new\nsection.\n\nSection two provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nAtlantic bonito and false albacore are currently unregulated, allowing\nthose who fish to keep as many as they want, at any size. No marine life\nspecies has been able to withstand fishing pressure to this extent. To\naddress this issue, several states along the East Coast have recently\nissued (MA), or are in the process of considering (NC, RI, CT), regu-\nlations on these species to prevent population declines and foster heal-\nthy, sustainable fisheries. These proactive regulatory measures make\nsense from an environmental perspective and are also being championed by\nsegments of the recreational fishing community and the American Saltwa-\nter Guides Association that are concerned about what will happen to\nfishing opportunities and the marine ecosystem if these species become\ndepleted.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThis is a new bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
